# AquaIntel — Sonar Pipeline (Part 1)
**Physics-Based, Retrieval-Driven Underwater Marine Debris and Anomaly Detection**  
*SIH 2026 | Problem Statement 26057 | Team Brainwave*

---

## Overview

AquaIntel treats side-scan sonar detection not as an uninterpretable black box, but as a physically grounded system where object identity stems from acoustic physics (shadow geometry $\to$ true physical height & morphology) feeding a retrieval and matching stage.

This module constitutes **Part 1 — Ingestion, Preprocessing & Physics Feature Engine**:
1. **Step 0 — Ingestion & Georeferencing**: Parses XTF, GeoTIFF, and PNG/NPY with JSON sidecars, extracting physical sensor metadata ($H_{\text{tow}}$, $R$, Heading, GPS) and resampling to a sensor-agnostic metric resolution ($0.05\,\text{m/px}$) with CRS-aware Affine georeferencing.
2. **Step 1 — Denoising & Motion Dropout Correction**: Suppresses multiplicative speckle noise via an Adaptive Lee Filter (with edge preservation) and corrects cross-ping motion dropouts ($\le 3$ rows linear 1D interpolation; $> 3$ rows masked as non-surveyable).
3. **Step 2 — Physics Feature Extraction**: Pairs acoustic highlights with their range shadows, computes true physical object heights using $\text{Height} = H_{\text{tow}} \times (L_{\text{shadow}} / R)$, extracts Haralick texture descriptors via scikit-image GLCM, and emits structured `SonarObjectFeature` records.

